    {
      "id": 477403,
      "username": "Hamza5",
      "name": "Hamza Abbad",
      "created_at": "2025-08-13T09:19:36.842Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I am getting a similar error “<strong>Field not permitted in query: tabXXX.</strong>”, where XXXX is the table name.</p>\n<p>This appeared when the doctype list was set to the image view in my case. This happened because I exported all rows of a doctype to CSV and removed them before changing the ID column then imported everything again. The attribute causing the problem was an image path, that I expected Frappe to cache the image internally even after removing the data, but it seems that all images were lost after removing the rows, so I need to re-upload them again.</p>\n<p>Also, at the end I had to run <code>bench migrate</code> to finally fix this error.</p>",
